{"name":"Hayden Valley","hex":"#5f5d50","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"valley","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elongated depression cast between hills or mountains, often with a river flowing through it.","An area which drains itself into a river."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form the shape of a valley."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valley"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hayden Valley","blocks":[{"text":"Hayden Valley is a large, sub-alpine valley within Yellowstone National Park straddling the Yellowstone River between Yellowstone Falls and Yellowstone Lake. The valley floor along the river is an ancient lake bed from a time when Yellowstone Lake was much larger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/HaydenValley1977JSchmidt.jpg/330px-HaydenValley1977JSchmidt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hayden_Valley","wikidata":"Q463354"},{"title":"Valley","blocks":[{"text":"A valley is an elongated low area often running between hills or mountains and typically containing a river or stream running from one end to the other. Most valleys are formed by erosion of the land surface by rivers or streams over a very long period. Some valleys are formed through erosion by glacial ice. These glaciers may remain present in valleys in high mountains or polar areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG/330px-Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley","wikidata":"Q39816"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Frosty_bison_in_the_road_on_a_cold_morning_in_Hayden_Valley_%2853482547136%29.jpg/500px-Frosty_bison_in_the_road_on_a_cold_morning_in_Hayden_Valley_%2853482547136%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&